# Paperclip itself stays keyless: it runs locally with no account and no key
# (npx paperclipai onboard --yes, default loopback mode).
#
# What changes in this course: the Worker you HIRE runs on a real model, so its
# runtime needs provider auth. You do NOT put that key here. You authenticate
# the local CLI the adapter spawns, and let it hold the credential:
#
#   claude_local    -> the `claude` CLI uses your Anthropic login (run `claude`
#                      once to sign in). Nothing to export for a default model.
#   opencode_local  -> authenticate `opencode` for the provider in your
#                      adapterConfig.model slug (e.g. `opencode auth login`),
#                      or export that provider's key in your shell.
#
# Never write a provider key into adapterConfig.env on a hire: Paperclip echoes
# adapterConfig.env back in plaintext on GET /api/agents/:id. Use the CLI's own
# auth, or Paperclip's secrets primitive. See AGENTS.md, "Secrets discipline".
#
# Nothing to fill in here. Keys live in your shell or the CLI's own auth store,
# never in this file or any committed file.
